How can we improve the accuracy of the sentimentAnalysis function in R for multiple sentences, accounting for punctuation and formatting variations in the input? Here is the sample code we have so far:
sentimentAnalysis <- function(input_text) {
  # Perform sentiment analysis using pre-trained model
  model <- sentiwordnet
  scores <- analyze(model, input_text)

  # Calculate score for positive, negative, and neutral sentiments
  pos_score <- scores$positive / (scores$positive + scores$negative + scores$objective)
  neg_score <- scores$negative / (scores$positive + scores$negative + scores$objective)
  neu_score <- scores$objective / (scores$positive + scores$negative + scores$objective)

  # Generate final score based on sentiment
  if pos_score > neg_score {
    score <- 1
  } else if neg_score > pos_score {
    score <- 0
  } else {
    score <- 0.5
  }

  return(score)
}
To handle multiple sentences and improve accuracy, we can add additional preprocessing steps to the input_text before passing it to the sentimentAnalysis function. For example, we can use regular expressions to remove punctuation and convert all text to lowercase. Here is the updated code:
sentimentAnalysis <- function(input_text) {
  # Preprocess input text
  input_text <- gsub("[[:punct:]]", "", input_text) # remove punctuation
  input_text <- tolower(input_text) # convert to lowercase

  # Perform sentiment analysis using pre-trained model
  model <- sentiwordnet
  scores <- analyze(model, input_text)

  # Calculate score for positive, negative, and neutral sentiments
  pos_score <- scores$positive / (scores$positive + scores$negative + scores$objective)
  neg_score <- scores$negative / (scores$positive + scores$negative + scores$objective)
  neu_score <- scores$objective / (scores$positive + scores$negative + scores$objective)

  # Generate final score based on sentiment
  if pos_score > neg_score {
    score <- 1
  } else if neg_score > pos_score {
    score <- 0
  } else {
    score <- 0.5
  }

  return(score)
}
Now, we can pass an array of sentences to the sentimentAnalysis function and the preprocessing steps will handle any punctuation and formatting variations.

