Sure, here's an Excel table that lists down the factors that affect the speed of wireless network connections and their impact on the network speed:
| Factors | Impact on Network Speed |
|---------|------------------------|
| Distance between device and router | The farther the distance, the slower the speed |
| Obstructions between device and router | Obstructions such as walls or furniture can slow down the speed |
| Interference from other wireless devices | Interference from other devices can cause slower speed |
| Network congestion | Too many devices using the network can slow down the speed |
| Router capabilities | Older routers may not support faster speeds |
As for the MATLAB code, here's an example code that can help you analyze the impact of these factors on your network speed:
```matlab
% Define the factors and their impact on network speed
distance = [1 2 3 4 5]; % Distance between device and router in meters
speed = [50 45 40 35 30]; % Speed in Mbps
obstruction = [0 1 2 3 4]; % Number of obstructions between device and router
interference = [0 1 2 3 4]; % Number of interfering devices
congestion = [0 1 2 3 4]; % Number of devices using the network
router = [1 2]; % Router capabilities (1 = old, 2 = new)
% Generate all possible combinations of the factors
factors = combvec(distance, obstruction, interference, congestion, router);
% Calculate the impact of each factor on network speed
impact = zeros(size(factors, 2), 1);
for i = 1:size(factors, 2)
    d = factors(1, i);
    o = factors(2, i);
    i = factors(3, i);
    c = factors(4, i);
    r = factors(5, i);

    % Calculate the speed based on the factors
    s = speed(distance == d) - o - i - c;
    if r == 1
        s = s * 0.5; % Reduce speed for old routers
    end

    impact(i) = impact(i) + s;
end
% Plot the impact of each factor on network speed
bar(impact);
xlabel('Factors');
ylabel('Impact on Network Speed');
title('Impact of Factors on Network Speed');
```
This code generates all possible combinations of the factors and calculates the impact of each factor on the network speed. It then plots the impact of each factor on the network speed. You can modify the values of the factors to analyze the impact on your network speed.

