Let's assume that there are 7 different types of fruits in the box, and let's denote the cost of each fruit as $x_1, x_2, ..., x_7$. 
We know that the total cost of the box after a 10% discount is $52.83. Therefore, the original cost of the box would be:
$$
\text{Original cost} = \frac{\text{Discounted cost}}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{52.83}{0.9} = 58.70
$$
Let's also assume that the tax rates for the 7 different types of fruits are given as percentages, and let's denote them as $t_1, t_2, ..., t_7$. 
To calculate the individual cost of each fruit, we can use the following system of equations:
\begin{align}
x_1 + x_2 + \cdots + x_7 &= 58.70 \\
t_1x_1 + t_2x_2 + \cdots + t_7x_7 &= 0.0625(0.9)(58.70) + 0.0725(0.9)(58.70) + \cdots + 0.0975(0.9)(58.70) \\
&= 3.778775
\end{align}
We can write this system of equations in matrix form as:
$$
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\
t_1 & t_2 & \cdots & t_7
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
x_1 \\
x_2 \\
\vdots \\
x_7
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
58.70 \\
3.778775
\end{bmatrix}
$$
We can solve for the vector of individual costs $\mathbf{x} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_7]^T$ using matrix inversion:
$$
\mathbf{x} = \begin{bmatrix}
1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\
t_1 & t_2 & \cdots & t_7
\end{bmatrix}^{-1}
\begin{bmatrix}
58.70 \\
3.778775
\end{bmatrix}
$$
The inverse of the matrix $\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\ t_1 & t_2 & \cdots & t_7 \end{bmatrix}$ can be computed using the formula:
$$
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\
t_1 & t_2 & \cdots & t_7
\end{bmatrix}^{-1}
=
\frac{1}{\Delta}
\begin{bmatrix}
\sum_{i=1}^7 t_i^2 & -\sum_{i=1}^7 t_i \\
-\sum_{i=1}^7 t_i & 7
\end{bmatrix}
$$
where $\Delta$ is the determinant of the matrix $\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\ t_1 & t_2 & \cdots & t_7 \end{bmatrix}$, which is given by:
$$
\Delta = \begin{vmatrix}
1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\
t_1 & t_2 & \cdots & t_7
\end{vmatrix}
= \sum_{i=1}^7 t_i \begin{vmatrix}
t_1 & \cdots & t_{i-1} & t_{i+1} & \cdots & t_7 \\
1 & \cdots & 1 & 1 & \cdots & 1
\end{vmatrix}
= \sum_{i=1}^7 t_i (-1)^{i+1} \begin{vmatrix}
1 & \cdots & 1 & 1 & \cdots & 1 \\
t_1 & \cdots & t_{i-1} & t_{i+1} & \cdots & t_7
\end{vmatrix}
$$
Using these formulas, we can compute the individual costs of the 7 different types of fruits.

