How can we implement a PHP function to translate the English statement "The dog is barking" into Spanish, considering grammatical tense and gender agreement? The function should allow for specification of whether the dog is a known or unknown entity and if any contextual information about the barking is relevant (e.g. warning or playful).
Here is an example PHP function that uses the Google Translate API to translate the statement:
```php
function translate($text, $known, $gender, $context) {
  $url = 'https://translation.googleapis.com/language/translate/v2';
  $data = array(
    'q' => $text,
    'source' => 'en',
    'target' => 'es',
    'format' => 'text',
    'model' => 'base',
    'key' => 'YOUR_API_KEY_HERE'
  );
  $options = array(
    'http' => array(
      'header'  => "Content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\r\n",
      'method'  => 'POST',
      'content' => http_build_query($data),
    ),
  );
  $context  = stream_context_create($options);
  $result = json_decode(file_get_contents($url, false, $context));
  $translation = $result->data->translations[0]->translatedText;

  if ($known) {
    if ($gender == 'male') {
      $translation = str_replace('el perro', 'el', $translation);
    } else if ($gender == 'female') {
      $translation = str_replace('el perro', 'la', $translation);
    }
  } else {
    if ($gender == 'male') {
      $translation = str_replace('un perro', 'un', $translation);
    } else if ($gender == 'female') {
      $translation = str_replace('un perro', 'una', $translation);
    }
  }
  if ($context == 'warning') {
    $translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando de forma amenazante', $translation);
  } else if ($context == 'playful') {
    $translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando juguetonamente', $translation);
  }
  return $translation;
}
```
The function takes in the English statement as a parameter, as well as the known/unknown status of the dog, gender of the dog, and context of the barking. It then uses the Google Translate API to translate the statement into Spanish, and modifies the translation based on the provided parameters.
To use the function, simply call it with the appropriate parameters, like this:
```php
$translation = translate('The dog is barking', true, 'male', 'warning');
echo $translation; // Output: El perro está ladrando de forma amenazante.
```

