To modify the PHP function to analyze the tone of a given text using the IBM Watson Tone Analyzer API, you can follow these steps:
1. Install the IBM Watson SDK for PHP by running the following command: `composer require ibm-watson/tone-analyzer-v3`
2. Create an instance of the Tone Analyzer service by passing your IBM Cloud credentials:
```
use IBM\Watson\ToneAnalyzerV3;
use IBM\Watson\Authenticator\IAMAuthenticator;
$authenticator = new IAMAuthenticator('<api_key>');
$toneAnalyzer = new ToneAnalyzerV3([
    'version' => '<version>',
    'authenticator' => $authenticator
]);
$toneAnalyzer->setServiceUrl('<service_url>');
```
3. Call the `tone()` method of the Tone Analyzer service to analyze the tone of the given text:
```
$text = 'Hello, how are you doing today?';
$toneAnalysis = $toneAnalyzer->tone([
    'text' => $text,
    'content_type' => 'text/plain'
]);
```
4. Categorize the tone data based on emotions, social tendencies, and language styles:
```
$tones = $toneAnalysis->getResult()->getDocumentTone()->getTones();
$emotions = [];
$socialTendencies = [];
$languageStyles = [];
foreach ($tones as $tone) {
    $category = $tone->getCategory()->getLabel();
    $toneName = $tone->getToneName();
    $score = $tone->getScore();
    switch ($category) {
        case 'Emotion Tone':
            $emotions[] = [
                'name' => $toneName,
                'score' => $score
            ];
            break;
        case 'Social Tone':
            $socialTendencies[] = [
                'name' => $toneName,
                'score' => $score
            ];
            break;
        case 'Language Tone':
            $languageStyles[] = [
                'name' => $toneName,
                'score' => $score
            ];
            break;
    }
}
```
5. Create an XML document using the SimpleXML extension and add the categorized tone data as child elements:
```
$xml = new SimpleXMLElement('<tone_analysis></tone_analysis>');
foreach ($emotions as $emotion) {
    $element = $xml->addChild('emotion');
    $element->addAttribute('name', $emotion['name']);
    $element->addAttribute('score', $emotion['score']);
}
foreach ($socialTendencies as $socialTendency) {
    $element = $xml->addChild('social_tendency');
    $element->addAttribute('name', $socialTendency['name']);
    $element->addAttribute('score', $socialTendency['score']);
}
foreach ($languageStyles as $languageStyle) {
    $element = $xml->addChild('language_style');
    $element->addAttribute('name', $languageStyle['name']);
    $element->addAttribute('score', $languageStyle['score']);
}
$xmlString = $xml->asXML();
```
6. The resulting XML data will look like this:
```
<tone_analysis>
    <emotion name="Anger" score="0.123456"/>
    <emotion name="Fear" score="0.234567"/>
    <social_tendency name="Openness" score="0.345678"/>
    <social_tendency name="Conscientiousness" score="0.456789"/>
    <language_style name="Analytical" score="0.567890"/>
    <language_style name="Confident" score="0.678901"/>
